00:49:41.300 --> 00:49:45.990
planned a celebration. I thought we could have a surprise party. It would be a lot of fun.

00:49:47.030 --> 00:49:57.970
And I had about 250 people on a list. I think he was surprised. He'd put on a good act if he wasn't.

00:50:02.080 --> 00:50:04.920
After almost everybody left, you know, I went up to him

00:50:04.920 --> 00:50:07.500
and congratulated him on his birthday and everything,

00:50:07.700 --> 00:50:13.710
and he hugged me, and he says, you know, I love you.

00:50:15.830 --> 00:50:17.690
And I said, I do too, Neil.

00:50:17.830 --> 00:50:18.930
We go back a long ways.

00:50:18.950 --> 00:50:19.910
He says, yeah, we do.

00:50:21.040 --> 00:50:22.120
That was the last time.

00:50:22.340 --> 00:50:29.600
On the 7th of August, 2008.

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:34.200
In 2012, Neil Armstrong was admitted to the hospital for heart surgery.

00:50:35.350 --> 00:50:39.120
He remained there until his death on August 25th.

00:50:41.160 --> 00:50:43.860
If there's a legacy, I think he may have left it already.

00:50:45.300 --> 00:50:54.040
He very much wanted the exploration of space to be an accomplishment that was important

00:50:54.040 --> 00:50:57.580
for this planet and everyone on it.

00:50:58.560 --> 00:50:59.620
his inspiration.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:10.720
to the generations that will follow is incalculable, I believe.

00:51:12.940 --> 00:51:17.880
It's overwhelming to think about how much has come from that inspiration.

00:51:19.930 --> 00:51:26.120
If there was something that he could pass along to future generations,

00:51:26.140 --> 00:51:29.430
I think it would be the conviction.

00:51:30.830 --> 00:51:32.070
to do the right thing.

00:51:32.310 --> 00:51:35.230
I mean, he went to the moon.

00:51:35.880 --> 00:51:38.140
He risked his life for the nation.

00:51:38.640 --> 00:51:41.900
And that would be reason enough to call Neil Armstrong a hero.

00:51:42.100 --> 00:51:45.860
But for me, the thing that really stands out

00:51:45.860 --> 00:51:49.740
is how he handled this role that fate gave him

00:51:49.960 --> 00:51:51.620
of being a world icon.

00:51:54.800 --> 00:51:56.740
One thing, he was true to himself.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:01.000
He was the man.

00:52:02.044 --> 00:52:03.044
that you saw.

00:52:05.852 --> 00:52:06.692
That was him.
